That's a very good point. Given the point of this whole thread, I
suppose the correct answer is "it would depend on the nature of the
deities in question."
I don't think it would be beyond the power of the gods to reshape the
terrain a little to their liking though. Items like "big axes and
shields" should probably remain unchanged (it is up to the guardians
of the temple, the priests, to provide suitable decorations) but any
deity-specific statues could be transmogrified. Some gods may even
chuck a few lightning bolts or fireballs about, just for effect. Since
we can guarnatee that that in the case of conversion the player will
definitely be standing on the altar, we can do what we like to the
other squares without risking instadeath. If the priest or your pets
or any other nearby monsters happen to get zapped/ drowned/ frozen/
boiled in lava/ crushed under boulders/ whatever then that may well be
in character for some gods. Other, more merciful, deities may find
ways of sparing innocent bystanders: teleporting them to safety before
remodelling, creating some extra land under the monster's feet or
whatever. Some might throw healing spells about rather than
pyrotechnics=-)
Again, the possibilities are nigh-limitless, and the potential for
special cases is sufficient to have even a non-coder like me reaching
for the aspirin, but it would definitely be cool.



